  "review_scope": "All 33 recursive author inputs receive a complete original read and two complete revised mathematical/editorial reads, including every proof. The second follows the first build and complete visual review. All 77 theorem/proposition/lemma/corollary/definition/example statements and all 157 previous labels are retained. After removing index commands, local spacing controls and whitespace, 74 of 76 proofs are unchanged; two proofs simplify their internal dependencies. The remaining problem is preserved. Chapter-local display pagination and short-statement guards are checked after the second read. All other author inputs and the bibliography are unchanged.",
  "mathematical_changes": "Chapter 25 now opens with the difference between fixed Kähler mass and the density-dependent Hermitian equation scalar, and distinguishes current attainment, smooth attainment and exact threshold equations. The integrable supporting-probability proof reuses the established directional-derivative argument after checking weighted-measure convergence and uniform Taylor expansion. Trace saturation invokes the selected-sequence attainment result directly. The divisorial discussion connects ordinary-type reduction to the exceptional density obstruction integrated in checkpoint211. Redundant closing inventories are removed and their remaining questions are placed beside the relevant results.",
  "mathematical_boundaries": "The full compact set of positive ddbar-closed currents remains distinct from the weak closure of smooth Gauduchon tests. Weighted tails give attainment and weighted-measure convergence, not smoothness. Smooth or analytically degenerate maximizing tests supply the additional rigidity for exact equations; smaller-background envelopes remain explicit extra hypotheses for capacity limits, and the moment theorem gives subsequential existence without whole-family uniqueness. Positive variational volume is not identified with bigness for a general nef background. Zero degeneration order does not imply positive limiting volume, and modification comparisons remain one-sided. Divisorial feasibility gives coefficient inequalities, whereas positive residual equations give the exact ordinary type. Necessary exceptional vanishing orders do not imply smoothness.",
  "dependencies": "Bounded external-to-unit reads cover the complete ordinary-divisor normalization and moving-family input in Chapter 14, the complete minimal exceptional-equation input in Chapter 13, and the exceptional-density obstruction and proof in Chapter 27. The unchanged positive-volume system recovery input in Chapter 29 is read for the interface; its hypotheses are not transferred to the variational-volume problem. The Chapter 24 ending and Chapter 26 opening are checked. The existing Gauduchon-volume history section is read at its bounded scope; no new external source-proof audit, independent verifier run or novelty claim is made.",
  "all_preexisting_formal_statements_unchanged_after_index_spacing_and_whitespace_normalization": true,
